/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope Envelope follower
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Analysis
 * @brief Follow a rectified signal with independent attack and release constants.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope_Goal Goal
 * Demonstrate asymmetric smoothing: a one-second attack rises to the expected
 * exponential fraction, while a two-second release decays at its own rate.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Analysis_Envelope_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Attack=1s after 1s: 632/1000; expected=632/1000
 * Release=2s after 2s: 233/1000; expected=233/1000
 * Zero time constants rectify immediately: input=-2 -> envelope=2
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * The last row makes the zero-time case explicit: no smoothing is requested,
 * but the envelope remains a magnitude and therefore rectifies the input.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope_Code Implementation
 * \include Analysis/Envelope/Shared.cpp
 */
